// Window and frame presentation.
//
// NOTE: on macOS this has no visible effect in a window. The system compositor
// vsyncs every windowed app to the display regardless of what the game asks for,
// so the frame rate stays pinned to the refresh rate (and on a ProMotion display
// varies between 60 and 120 on its own). Verified by measurement, not assumed.
// The setting still matters on Windows and Linux.
(
    // Vsync   - capped to your display's refresh rate, no tearing. Recommended.
    //           On an adaptive-refresh display (ProMotion, FreeSync, G-Sync) the
    //           driver already drops the rate when nothing is moving, which is
    //           better than a fixed cap: full smoothness while you are dragging
    //           the camera, low power when you are not.
    // NoVsync - uncapped. Lowest input latency, may tear, works the GPU hardest.
    // Mailbox - vsync without the frame cap, where the platform supports it.
    present_mode: Vsync,
)
